WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.913 --> 00:00:08.815
Once upon a time, there was a young boy.

2
00:00:09.896 --> 00:00:12.899
He lived in a quiet village where many people owned sheep.

3
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.062
The boy's job was to watch all the sheep.

4
00:00:18.404 --> 00:00:20.526
He had to protect them from hungry wolves.

5
00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:26.352
Looking after the sheep was easy, but it wasn't fun.

6
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.882
"I'm so bored," he thought.

7
00:00:32.902 --> 00:00:36.844
"I wish something exciting would happen."

8
00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.109
One day the boy had an idea.

9
00:00:47.132 --> 00:00:48.432
He took a deep breath.

10
00:00:48.452 --> 00:00:50.774
"A wolf!"

11
00:00:51.355 --> 00:00:51.895
he shouted.

12
00:00:51.915 --> 00:00:55.417
"Help! There's a wolf!"

13
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.201
The whole village heard the boy's cry.

14
00:01:04.382 --> 00:01:06.343
Everyone ran to the boy in fright.

15
00:01:12.506 --> 00:01:12.926
is it?

16
00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.446
Where's the wolf?"

17
00:01:14.867 --> 00:01:15.967
an old man asked.

18
00:01:18.108 --> 00:01:20.549
The boy shrugged and tried to hide his grin.

19
00:01:20.569 --> 00:01:24.211
"Um I guess it ran away."

20
00:01:24.231 --> 00:01:27.172
The villagers frowned.

21
00:01:28.504 --> 00:01:29.744
No one believed the boy.

22
00:01:30.985 --> 00:01:31.845
But what could they say?

23
00:01:31.865 --> 00:01:37.246
The next day the boy was watching the sheep again.

24
00:01:37.266 --> 00:01:41.708
"Yesterday was fun," he thought.

25
00:01:41.728 --> 00:01:46.049
He giggled as he thought about how he had tricked the villagers.

26
00:01:46.069 --> 00:01:48.790
"I'll do it again!"

27
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.171
The boy took a deep breath.

28
00:01:52.191 --> 00:01:54.451
"A wolf!"

29
00:01:54.991 --> 00:01:55.511
he shouted.

30
00:01:55.531 --> 00:01:58.948
"Help! There's a wolf!"

31
00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.590
The frightened villagers ran to the boy and looked around.

32
00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.851
"Where's the wolf?"

33
00:02:08.231 --> 00:02:09.311
a shopkeeper cried.

34
00:02:09.331 --> 00:02:12.532
"Yes, where is it?"

35
00:02:12.872 --> 00:02:14.533
the old man asked, frowning.

36
00:02:16.153 --> 00:02:17.394
The boy hid his grin.

37
00:02:17.414 --> 00:02:22.015
"It was just here, and then it ran off."

38
00:02:23.315 --> 00:02:24.596
The old man sighed.

39
00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.021
"Never cry 'Wolf!'

40
00:02:28.241 --> 00:02:29.942
when there is no wolf."

41
00:02:30.963 --> 00:02:32.063
The villagers nodded.

42
00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:34.765
"That's a bad idea, boy!"

43
00:02:37.686 --> 00:02:40.107
After everyone left, the boy burst out laughing.

44
00:02:43.289 --> 00:02:44.770
Baa! Baa!

45
00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:46.851
Suddenly he heard the sheep.

46
00:02:48.212 --> 00:02:49.012
The boy gulped.

47
00:02:50.173 --> 00:02:51.894
A big wolf was chasing the sheep!

48
00:02:53.895 --> 00:02:54.695
"A wolf!"

49
00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:55.896
the boy shouted.

50
00:02:56.828 --> 00:02:58.549
"Help! There's a wolf!

51
00:02:59.109 --> 00:03:04.711
Really!" All of the villagers heard the boy crying "Wolf!"

52
00:03:05.892 --> 00:03:08.513
But this time they were not going to fall for his trick.

53
00:03:09.674 --> 00:03:11.254
So everyone ignored his shouts.

54
00:03:15.636 --> 00:03:18.177
In the evening the villagers came to check on their sheep.

55
00:03:19.738 --> 00:03:20.958
But the sheep were gone.

56
00:03:22.439 --> 00:03:24.440
The wolf had eaten them all up.

57
00:03:29.324 --> 00:03:30.565
The shopkeeper gasped.

58
00:03:30.585 --> 00:03:32.927
"Where are the sheep?"

59
00:03:32.947 --> 00:03:36.450
"I called 'Wolf!'

60
00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.993
but nobody came to help me," the boy said.

61
00:03:40.013 --> 00:03:43.736
"Of course nobody came to help you!"

62
00:03:44.077 --> 00:03:45.197
the old man snapped.

63
00:03:46.679 --> 00:03:48.240
The shopkeeper glared at the boy.

64
00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.142
"You tricked us twice!"

65
00:03:53.585 --> 00:03:54.705
The old man nodded.

66
00:03:54.725 --> 00:03:57.488
"You called 'Wolf!'

67
00:03:57.748 --> 00:03:59.610
when there was no wolf!"

68
00:04:01.632 --> 00:04:02.854
The boy hung his head.

69
00:04:02.874 --> 00:04:10.362
"Sorry." "You learned something today," the old man said.

70
00:04:11.363 --> 00:04:16.148
"Nobody believes a liar, even when a liar tells the truth!"
